# Sugar-water tower: measure the ordering before trying to stack it
register lv2

# Equal starting water, increasing sugar. The density readings are the
# computed evidence for which solution belongs at the bottom.
add v1 water 100mL
measure v1 density

new cylinder
add v2 water 100mL
add v2 table_sugar 25g
measure v2 density

new cylinder
add v3 water 100mL
add v3 table_sugar 50g
measure v3 density

# The ordering is computed. A real tower also needs a gentle delivery that
# preserves a vertical concentration gradient. This bench has no slow-pour
# operation or diffusion state, so it does not draw layers it cannot retain.
